{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161145-theory-about-the-hosts","id":161145,"title":"Theory About the Hosts..","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-06T14:46:13-07:00","id":161145,"title":"Theory About the Hosts..","content":"This story can't be true..<br /> <br /> Or can it?<br /> <br /> So, the Hosts are, in essence, shards of powerful spirits in physical forms. Each of those spirits apparently was hunted by Father Wolf, and scattering its Essence was its only way to survive. Also, it was hinted that those spirits were a part of some &quot;pantheon&quot;, and so they were connected to each other. We also know that one of them, the make of the Locust Host, is still alive. We also know that it is an idigam, which may be the reason for how it survived- after all, the Moon Banished are the spirits who who father wold couldn't kill. Now, if all the Progenitors were a part of the same &quot;pantheon&quot;, it may mean that all of the Hosts come from idigams, which may sound logical, considering the feat needed to manipulate Essence in such a way. Yet, if the idigams are things Father Wolf couldn't kill- than how the Spinner Hag and the Plague King has died? I mean, having one such Progenitor surviving is cool. Having them all waiting on the Moon kinda misses the point.<br /> <br /> Sure, maybe not all of them are idigams- but if they are, than how did they died?<br /> <br /> Simply- they didn't.<br /> <br /> Or, more exactly, there are no &quot;they&quot;. There is just one.<br /> <br /> So, here is the idea- the idigams are changing by their nature, right? This is why they could avoid getting killed by Father Wolf. In that case, maybe the one behind all of those hosts is simply the same idigam, which changed its form again and again while trying to escape the claws of the great Wolfand each time it was defeated it left a chunk of itself behind, which turned into an Host based around its last form it had when it &quot;died&quot;. Eventually, it was thrown to the Moon while wearing its last form- a Locust- and that was the last Host to be formed. That means that the wishes of the Hosts to unite and recreating themselves are lost cause- for their maker is still alive, and all they do is trying to create a false image of it. It also mean that the idigam has played a long game of tag with Father Wolf, and maybe now that it returned, it wishes to play again- with his children.<br /> <br /> so.. thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T07:21:33-07:00","id":161689,"title":"","content":"Convoluted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T07:52:01-07:00","id":161715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/161145-theory-about-the-hosts?p=161689#post161689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Convoluted.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, it's pretty straightforward. All the hosts were created by one Idigam. Simple, and not unreasonable if you want to make a single Big Bad. Don't confuse LostLight's explanation of his reasoning behind the theory for the theory itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T08:47:45-07:00","id":161775,"title":"","content":"And even if it was, there's nothing wrong with convoluted myths. Mythologies aren't supposed to make sense or be coherent or answer all questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T09:21:21-07:00","id":161795,"title":"","content":"I am a fan of the more canonical explanations behind the Host's birth so this theory is not my cup of tea but it is good, especially in a Shartha heavy game. It allows to have a single greater antagonist and to feature lots of multiple Hosts without the players going &quot;these things are supposed to be rare, but it seems every big animal spirit in Pangea knew how to make its own&quot;, which admittedly is a risk when using the Shartha a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T09:47:43-07:00","id":161811,"title":"","content":"Well- I did thought about it while going back from work, so it is pretty raw. Plus, I'm also a fan for &quot;each Host its own maker&quot; thing- but the fact that it is a possibility, a story, a myth. Something a lonely Bone Shadow may think about, or a story told by an ancient spirit, or something like that. It is meant to make things weirder. After all- this story can't be true.. but what if it is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T12:58:43-07:00","id":161941,"title":"","content":"I see a story hook of someone who believes this and is relentlessly searching for said Idigam's ban.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-07T21:41:15-07:00","id":162197,"title":"","content":"It is possible, but Idigam or not, most spirits wouldn't survive that many deaths at the fangs and claws of what could arguably of been a rank 7- 8 spirit such as Urfarah. Not saying that it is impossible, the very fact that Father Wolf had to lock them upon the moon is a testament to the trickiness of the Idigam, it makes more sense if it was several spirits in stead of a single being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T08:46:34-07:00","id":162431,"title":"","content":"As a theory a Bone Shadow may tell or something a spirit can blurt when speaking with the Uratha, it's perfect. I don't have anything bad to say about it. It is not unreasonable for a werewolf (probably a slightly subversive one, who has not as many respect for myths as the others) to come up with this idea.<br /> <br /> After all, Uratha can't just go to DrivethruRPG and buy some pdfs to get the &quot;right&quot; informations <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-08T09:05:17-07:00","id":162437,"title":"","content":"Intriguing notion. Where my brain goes is, what if it goes a step further? So there was this idigam, constantly getting attacked by Urfara, and having to leave chunks of itself behind, which became greater entities in their own right. Over and over again. Almost, like a cycle? Chase, break, escape. Now, assuming that this idigam progenitor was clever, likely it would have foreseen this, maybe even intended for it, using Urfara by predicting and playing off his essential nature. So, what was its plan?<br /> <br /> And take it one step further. Co-ordination between spirits is rare, unless there's some connection, usually they're of the same type or choir. Doesn't that imply something about Urfara?<br /> <br /> Just something that occurred to me while reading your theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}